  "body": "`src/logger.ts` had no JSDoc. The issue also asked why every level calls `console.error` instead of `console.info`, `console.warn` and `console.debug`. This PR adds JSDoc and keeps the `console.error` calls on purpose. It only adds comments; runtime behaviour is unchanged.\n\n### Changes\n- **JSDoc**: covers `LOG_LEVELS`, the `Logger` class and constructor, `setLevel`, the private `shouldLog`, every level method (prefix, colour, threshold) and the exported `logger` singleton.\n- **stderr rationale** (class-level doc): in Node, `console.info` and `console.debug` write to stdout. `awf` wraps a user command whose stdout is often piped or parsed, so logs must not mix into it. Sending every level to stderr keeps stdout clean.\n\n```ts\n/**\n * All messages are written to stderr via `console.error`, regardless of level.\n * This is intentional: in Node.js, `console.info` and `console.debug` write to\n * stdout, which would interleave log lines with the stdout of the command\n * wrapped by awf and break callers that parse or pipe that output.\n */\nclass Logger {\n```\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes #9067",
